<article class="site-article">
  <h1>About WannaWatch</h1>
  <p class="lede">Movie night shouldn’t start with twenty minutes of scrolling and negotiating. WannaWatch turns “what do you wanna watch?” into a quick, shared swipe.</p>

  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>WannaWatch is a free web app where friends join the same game, swipe through the same deck of movies and shows, and match when everyone likes the same title. The first mutual match is tonight’s pick.</p>

  <h2>Who it’s for</h2>
  <p>Couples, roommates, friend groups, and anyone tired of the streaming paradox of choice. Play in a browser on your phone or laptop — no account required to start, though a free login helps you keep friends, history, and purchases.</p>

  <h2>What stays free</h2>
  <p>Core play stays free: create or join a game, swipe together, match, and invite friends. Free play may show light ads (including occasional breaks between swipes). WannaWatch+ is $2.99/month for no ads, Fine-tune filters, and full history — not a paywall for matching. Cancel anytime.</p>

  <h2>Movie data</h2>
  <p>Titles, posters, and related details come from <a href="https://www.themoviedb.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">The Movie Database (TMDB)</a>. WannaWatch is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.</p>

  <p><a class="site-cta" href="/">Start a game</a> · <a href="/how-it-works">See how it works</a></p>
